               </text>
            </section>
            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your patient, a 75-year-old female, admitted on 15/08/2008 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed mild hypoxaemia. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and monitored continuously with pulse oximetry. Vital signs were closely observed throughout her stay. She responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. She was discharged on 16/08/2008 with an oral steroid taper and optimised inhaler regimen. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
